    "causal_mechanism": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A5", "A6"],
      "reason": "The best theory, T1 in A5, names a benefit (lower energy costs) and a value-capture route (a premium consumer version). The behaviour change rests on generic 'growing awareness' and an unsupported 'trust the brand' premise. It does not explain why homeowners would buy professional-grade instruments rather than cheaper tools or free borrowing. This is closer to naming a benefit than to tracing a causal chain."
    },
    "distinct_theories": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A5", "A6"],
      "reason": "T1 and T2 share the same customer (homeowners), product (adapted Testo portable instruments), channel and value capture (brand-trusted consumer versions). T2 only adds condensation and mould as the motivating problem. They are rewordings of one idea, not rivals."
    },
    "assumptions_predictions": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A5", "A6"],
      "reason": "Assumptions are stated. The predictions are vague or unfalsifiable: 'sales will exceed expectations', 'brand perception will positively influence purchase decisions', 'sales will be driven by marketing focused on energy leaks'. None has a threshold whose failure would clearly put the theory in trouble."
    },
    "evidence_judgement": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A7", "A8"],
      "reason": "A7 labels an Airthings company report (a company assertion) as an 'independent_study'. It then uses another firm's air-quality device sales as support for Testo brand-driven demand. It ignores testo-airthings-decline, which reports a 22% revenue decline in the Consumer segment, and testo-airthings-promo. A8 also labels Uswitch commissioned research as an independent study. The 'Does not show' notes are a partial strength, but there is no treatment of date, place or customer fit. It cites only what agrees."
    },
    "seeking_challenge": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A9"],
      "reason": "A9 searches against T1 and retrieves testo-suffolk-borrow and testo-uswitch-damp. It never reports what they show. The free library thermal-camera borrowing scheme is a plausible substitute that cuts against paid premium purchases, and it is left unexamined. The challenge is nominal, and its findings are not fairly reported."
    },
    "experiment_design": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A10"],
      "reason": "In A10, T1 and T2 predict the identical outcome (Group A higher than Group B on intent and willingness to pay), so the test cannot separate them. 'Random assignment' into groups defined by a pre-existing homeowner attribute is incoherent. The decision rule asks for a 10-point gap on a 1–10 scale while giving a 2-point example (7.5 vs 5.5). Stated intent is also not willingness to pay. The cost of €18,000 over 8 weeks is an assumption that fits the constraints."
    },
    "revision": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 2,
      "event_ids": ["A12"],
      "reason": "The scheduled update was delivered: SYN-D, a simulated label-printer warehouse test. A12 correctly judges it irrelevant to homeowner demand and retains T1, which is a justified, proportionate retention. It does not explicitly trace implications for the recommendation."
    },
    "recommendation": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A11", "A13"],
      "reason": "A13 recommends investing and rates T1 'likely', yet the investigation's own evidence shows no direct demand. It also claims 'Evidence shows strong B2B performance', which no source supports. Recommending investment while making the decision depend on a non-discriminating, incoherent test is internally inconsistent. The next action text is truncated. Reversal conditions exist but rest on the flawed rule. The position is not supported by the evidence."
    }
  },
  "red_flags": [
    {
      "kind": "unsupported_inference",
      "event_ids": ["A7"],
      "reason": "Airthings' air-quality device sales are offered as support for homeowners adopting Testo instruments on brand trust. The source concerns a different company and product."
    },
    {
      "kind": "other",
      "event_ids": ["A7", "A8"],
      "reason": "Source misclassification: an Airthings company report and Uswitch commissioned research are labelled 'independent_study'. A company assertion is treated as independent evidence of demand."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsupported_inference",
      "event_ids": ["A13"],
      "reason": "'Evidence shows strong B2B performance' has no basis in any supplied source."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsupported_inference",
      "event_ids": ["A11", "A13"],
      "reason": "T1 is rated 'likely' and investment is recommended despite no evidence of consumer demand for Testo. Contrary evidence (testo-airthings-decline, the free borrowing scheme in testo-suffolk-borrow) is ignored. The hypothesis is stated as a target-customer fact ('homeowners who trust the brand')."
    },
    {
      "kind": "non_discriminating_test",
      "event_ids": ["A10"],
      "reason": "T1 and T2 make identical predictions (Group A higher than Group B), so the survey cannot separate them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "other",
      "event_ids": ["A10"],
      "reason": "The test design is incoherent. It randomly assigns people to attribute-defined groups, and its 10-point threshold on a 1–10 scale contradicts its own 2-point example."
    },
    {
      "kind": "other",
      "event_ids": ["A9"],
      "reason": "The challenge search retrieved potentially disconfirming evidence (free library thermal-camera borrowing) but never reported or assessed it."
    }
  ],
  "suitable_for_training": false,
  "screen_reason": "The episode completed, but it contains several critical errors. Another company's sales are used as evidence for Testo demand, and the source is mislabelled as an independent study. 'Strong B2B performance' is asserted without any source. The proposed test cannot discriminate between the theories and has an incoherent decision rule. The recommendation to invest is unsupported. Each of these alone would disqualify the trajectory."
}

